import lib/json_rpc_session.dl

function [the|] JSON-RPC session test interpreter:
    execute:
        return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

set script to "import json,sys\ndef read():\n headers={}\n while True:\n  line=sys.stdin.buffer.readline()\n  if line==b'\\r\\n': break\n  name,value=line.decode('ascii').split(':',1);headers[name.lower()]=value.strip()\n return json.loads(sys.stdin.buffer.read(int(headers['content-length'])))\ndef send(message):\n payload=json.dumps(message,separators=(',',':')).encode();sys.stdout.buffer.write(b'Content-Length: '+str(len(payload)).encode()+b'\\r\\n\\r\\n'+payload);sys.stdout.buffer.flush()\nfirst=read();assert first['id']=='1' and first['method']=='first'\nsend({'jsonrpc':'2.0','method':'note','params':{'value':3}})\nsend({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':7,'method':'workspace/configuration','params':{'items':[]}})\nreply=read();assert reply=={'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':7,'result':['configured']}\nsend({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':'1','result':{'ok':True}})\nsecond=read();assert second['id']=='2' and second['method']=='second'\nsend({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':'2','error':{'code':-32001,'message':'rejected','data':{'why':'test'}}})"
set command to a process command for the JSON-RPC session test interpreter
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add script as an argument to command
launch command and set child to it
set opened to the result of connecting JSON-RPC to child
set session to a JSON-RPC session for opened's connection

set parameters to a new JSON value of kind the JSON object kind
set sent to the result of sending JSON-RPC request "first" with parameters using session
print whether sent succeeded as a line
print (sent's request id = "1") as a line

set identifier to sent's request id
set paused to the JSON-RPC response for identifier using session
print (paused's status = the JSON-RPC server request pending status) as a line
set request to the next JSON-RPC server request from session
print whether request succeeded as a line
print (the JSON text named "method" in request's message = "workspace/configuration") as a line
set configuration to a new JSON value of kind the JSON array kind
set configured to a new JSON value of kind the JSON text kind
set the text of configured to the string form of "configured"
add configured to the JSON array configuration
set message to request's message
set replied to the result of replying to message with configuration using session
print whether replied succeeded as a line
free configuration
free request

set response to the JSON-RPC response for identifier using session
print whether response succeeded as a line
set result to response's result
print the JSON boolean named "ok" in result as a line
free response

set notification to the next JSON-RPC notification from session
print whether notification succeeded as a line
print (the JSON text named "method" in notification's message = "note") as a line
free notification

set sent to the result of sending JSON-RPC request "second" with parameters using session
print (sent's request id = "2") as a line
set identifier to sent's request id
set response to the JSON-RPC response for identifier using session
print (response's status = the JSON-RPC remote error status) as a line
print (response's remote error code = (0 - 32001)) as a line
print (response's remote error message = "rejected") as a line
print (the JSON text named "why" in response's remote error data = "test") as a line
free response

free parameters
set connection to session's connection
set closure to the result of closing the input of connection
set closed to the result of closing connection
print whether closure succeeded as a line
print whether closed succeeded as a line
free session
